### Current Picture of the Water Guild

- **Name feel**: Cellar Custodians (working title still open)
- **Aesthetic**: Grease-monkey / boiler-room practical. Heavy boots, stained canvas, tool belts, heat-resistant gloves. Militaristic organization and discipline.
- **Core work**: Mechanical pump condensers, boiler rooms, and long subterranean tunnels lined with hot and cold pipes.
- **Hidden function**: Several deep stations that condition and distribute a second set of “ingredients” through the city’s water network — a cooled, diluted form of the same binding force the Weavers handle in thread form.
- **Overlap**: Weaver threads already follow many of the same utility pathways, so the two guilds share tunnels and must coordinate (or carefully ignore each other).
- **Threat environment**: The deep tunnels have a serious pest problem. Many of the “common” subterranean creatures are fully capable of killing an adult human. This is one reason the Custodians are organized more like a combat brigade than a normal utility crew.

This gives them a very different flavour from the Weavers: hotter, louder, more physical, and more openly dangerous.

